    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "e8nk207",
      "content": "<strong>UNIT 3 — ENGLISH LANGUAGE</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b2wauey",
      "content": "The English Language section tests reading comprehension, grammar, vocabulary, and verbal ability. PSU CBT exams typically have 15–30 questions. Key topics: Reading Comprehension, Synonyms &amp; Antonyms, Fill in the Blanks, Error Detection, Para-jumbles, Idioms &amp; Phrases, One-word Substitution, and Sentence Correction."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "obyx4vf",
      "content": "<strong>3.1  Grammar Essentials</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sacjzdq",
      "content": "<strong>Parts of Speech</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "y7kucoi",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Part of Speech</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Definition</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Noun</p>",
            "<p>Name of a person, place, thing or idea</p>",
            "<p>BEL, NALCO, engineer, courage</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pronoun</p>",
            "<p>Replaces a noun</p>",
            "<p>he, she, they, it, we</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Verb</p>",
            "<p>Action or state of being</p>",
            "<p>run, is, achieve, manage</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Adjective</p>",
            "<p>Describes a noun</p>",
            "<p>excellent, large, technical</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Adverb</p>",
            "<p>Modifies a verb, adjective or adverb</p>",
            "<p>quickly, very, almost</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Preposition</p>",
            "<p>Shows relationship between noun and rest of sentence</p>",
            "<p>in, on, at, for, with</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Conjunction</p>",
            "<p>Connects words, phrases or clauses</p>",
            "<p>and, but, or, although, because</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Interjection</p>",
            "<p>Expresses emotion</p>",
            "<p>Oh!, Wow!, Alas!</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "i6tqq2o",
      "content": "<strong>Subject–Verb Agreement</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "hngnop6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Singular subject takes singular verb: \"The engineer works hard.\"",
        "Plural subject takes plural verb: \"The engineers work hard.\"",
        "Compound subjects joined by \"and\" take plural verb: \"Ram and Shyam are working.\"",
        "When joined by \"or/nor\", verb agrees with the nearer subject: \"Neither he nor they are correct.\"",
        "Collective nouns (committee, team, jury) take singular verb when acting as one unit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7ditvnn",
      "content": "<strong>Tenses Quick Reference</strong>"
